dialect protocol
protocol stdio.gif.diff
version 1
schema stdio.gif.diff
start diff

# Real binary diff-frame `protocol::DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff` NOW emit for
# `GifDiff` — upgraded, this program (P2-FG2), from the F6-era `print_diff().into_bytes()`
# text-as-binary shortcut (see this artifact's report; the FG1 wave's own closer report
# flagged leaving this un-upgraded as a real defect to not repeat). `GifDiff` is a STRUCT
# (not an enum) with a mix of PLAIN `Option<T>` fields (`width`/`height`/
# `background_color_index`/`pixel_aspect_ratio`/`images`) and ONE TRI-STATE
# `Option<Option<T>>` field (`gct`) — so every field gets its own presence-FLAG byte, directly
# modeling M2's real conditional-field-presence mechanism (item 4): a plain field uses a
# 2-way flag (`0`=unchanged, `1`=changed); the tri-state `gct` field uses a 3-way flag
# (`0`=unchanged, `1`=cleared-to-None, `2`=set-to-Some(value)) rather than TWO chained
# `if`-guarded fields — chaining would need a second field's `if` guard to reference a field
# that was ITSELF only conditionally decoded (the outer flag), and `eval_cond` unconditionally
# errors ("condition references unknown field") when its guarded field was never read
# (confirmed by reading `eval_cond`/`walk_fields`, `📖️grammar/🦀️.rs`) — a real,
# concrete instance of this artifact's report `mechanism_gaps` entry
# `protocol-cond-cannot-chain` (PNG's own precedent). The single-flat-flag-per-field design
# below sidesteps it entirely (every `if` guard here references a field that is ALWAYS
# unconditionally read, one line above).
#
# `gct` (variable-length: `GifColorTable` has a Vec of RGB triples) and `images` (the
# `removed`/`modified`/`added` collection triple, itself containing recursively-nested
# `GifImage`/`GifImageDiff` values) are both length-prefixed opaque byte blobs (`<name>_len
# varint` + `Array(u8, Field(<name>_len))`) — `Prim::Ref` to a struct/enum still
# unconditionally errors at walk time (confirmed unchanged since P2-M2, `protocol-prim-ref-
# recursion`), so their own internal shape isn't further protocol-walkable; the Rust
# `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` side (`../🦀️.rs`'s `RealBinaryDiffFrame`/
# `RealBinaryPrimitives` regions) IS genuinely, fully structured real binary (real varint
# counts, real per-item recursive encoding) — this is purely a limit on how deep the PROTOCOL
# DESCRIPTION itself can validate structurally, same documented limitation as every other
# stdio pilot's own nested-payload field.
framing record

field width_flag u8
field width_value u32 if width_flag eq 1
field height_flag u8
field height_value u32 if height_flag eq 1

field gct_flag u8
field gct_len varint if gct_flag eq 2
field gct_value Array(u8, Field(gct_len)) if gct_flag eq 2

field background_color_index_flag u8
field background_color_index_value u8 if background_color_index_flag eq 1
field pixel_aspect_ratio_flag u8
field pixel_aspect_ratio_value u8 if pixel_aspect_ratio_flag eq 1

field images_flag u8
field images_len varint if images_flag eq 1
field images_value Array(u8, Field(images_len)) if images_flag eq 1
